  ],
  "description": "Trident A-Range channel module Type 1038, drawing ED3001. Four-band equalizer from the high-pass amplifier feed at C26 to the midrange amplifier output at C46. The two discrete Class A amplifiers use the BC413 group B nominal current gain and an effective MPSA12 Darlington transport card with two forward junction drops. Nominal regulated supply 30 V, source 47 Ω, test load 100 kΩ. The four center-detented faders increase from cut through flat to boost. Frequency range and step switches encode the four original contacts from low to high. Low shelf 50/80/100/150 Hz, low mid 250/500/1000/2000 Hz, high mid 3/5/7/9 kHz, high shelf 8/10/12/15 kHz. L1 tap inductances are inferred from the printed switch frequencies and capacitors; series sections preserve each selected tap impedance. L2 uses an estimated 50/120 mH coupled winding. Coil resistances and transistor transport parameters are estimates. The separate high- and low-pass stages sit outside the selected terminals.",
  "io": {
    "groundNode": "0",
    "inputNode": "in",
    "outputNode": "midOut"
  },
